  },
  {
    "id": 19,
    "question": "How does the FAQ chatbot with TF-IDF and Cosine Similarity work?",
    "answer": "The FAQ chatbot works by first preprocessing both the user's input and the FAQ questions using NLP techniques like tokenization and lemmatization. Then, it converts the text into numerical vectors using TF-IDF Vectorizer. Finally, it computes the Cosine Similarity between the user's question vector and each FAQ question vector to find the best match. If the similarity score is above a threshold, it returns the matched FAQ answer; otherwise, it falls back to an LLM for a generated response."
  },
  {
    "id": 20,
    "question": "What happens if I fail to complete a task in the CodeAlpha AI Internship?",
