  },
  {
    "id": 21,
    "question": "What is the LLM fallback mechanism in the FAQ chatbot?",
    "answer": "The LLM fallback mechanism is a feature of the FAQ chatbot that activates when the Cosine Similarity score between the user's question and the best-matching FAQ falls below a threshold (typically 0.60). Instead of returning a potentially irrelevant FAQ answer, the chatbot forwards the user's question to an LLM API (like ChatGPT-4o) which generates a conversational and contextually appropriate response. This ensures the chatbot always provides helpful answers."
  },
  {
    "id": 22,
    "question": "What is the format of the certificate from CodeAlpha?",
    "answer": "The CodeAlpha internship certificate is a digitally verifiable certificate that includes your name, the internship program name, duration, and a unique verification code. It can be downloaded as a PDF and shared on LinkedIn, added to your resume, or included in your portfolio. The certificate serves as proof of your practical experience in AI and machine learning."
  },
