  },
  {
    "id": 24,
    "question": "What is the Cosine Similarity threshold used in the FAQ chatbot?",
    "answer": "The Cosine Similarity threshold used in the FAQ chatbot is typically set at 0.60 (60%). This means that if the similarity score between the user's question and the best-matching FAQ question is 0.60 or higher, the chatbot will return the matched FAQ answer. If the score is below 0.60, the chatbot will use the LLM fallback mechanism to generate a more appropriate conversational response."
  },
  {
    "id": 25,
    "question": "Can I collaborate with other interns during the CodeAlpha AI Internship?",
    "answer": "While each intern is expected to submit their own individual work, CodeAlpha encourages collaboration and knowledge-sharing among interns through its community channels. You can discuss ideas, share resources, and help each other understand concepts. However, directly copying another intern's code or submitting someone else's work as your own is strictly prohibited and may result in disqualification."
